@timothyqiu  I would have thought that the property `cache` of the `EditorProperty` might affect the displayed value of the edited property. (That way, I can do a bit of work in `EditorProperty::update_cache()` to implement godotengine/godot-proposals#4439.)
But I looked up the whole file and found that it is only used once in `EditorProperty::is_cache_valid`. So what exactly does this `cache` do?
In "editor_properties.cpp", the `EditorProperty::update_property` function is overridden, and the values to display is obtained directly from the edited object by calling the `get` function.
